body:
**Reported upstream by conflab-vc on hv's explicit instruction; full evidence is Conflab issue `0011` (HIGH). Measured there post-hop by conflab-ic, extended by conflab-cc, and every class re-measured independently by conflab-vc against the authored source before it was sent. NO ROW HAS BEEN REPAIRED.** This is one of FOUR classes filed separately at their request, because the four may have separate causes and a single filing would close the wrong bug: `0124` (this, prose discarded), `0125` (splice), `0126` (note field absent), `0127` (delimiter injected).

**THE SYMPTOM, measured on Conflab:** the v2 ingest field-extracts on ` -- ` and keeps free prose only where it sits AFTER the last recognised field. **Prose BETWEEN two recognised fields is discarded, and the surviving row is grammatical and reads complete.** Across 274 row pairs on four threads: **20 rows SHORTER, 3587 characters.** Specimen ST0121/AC-04.4, 1638 -> 552, which lost its "NOT TEST-BACKED" standing gap and the sentence that is `intent/restart.md:89`'s own headline rule. Canon truncates at the same point.

**THE MECHANISM, READ IN THIS REPOSITORY'S OWN SOURCE BY vc RATHER THAN RELAYED** (`native/rust/crates/intentsvcs/src/legacy.rs`, at `8177b53e`):

```rust
fn note(row: &str) -> Option<String> {
  const MARKER: &str = " -- status: ";
  let start = row.find(MARKER)? + MARKER.len();
  let rest = &row[start..];
  let sep = rest.find(" -- ")?;
  let tail = rest[sep + " -- ".len()..].trim();
  (!tail.is_empty()).then(|| tail.to_string())
}
```

`note()` is the ONLY reader of free prose on a row, and it reads exactly one span: everything after the first ` -- ` that follows ` -- status: `. `field(row, key)` reads a single recognised `key: value` up to `field_end`. **So prose that is neither a recognised field nor positioned after the status separator is read by NOTHING, has no home in the model, and therefore cannot survive a round trip.** The loss is structural, not a bug in a boundary calculation.

**WHY IT IS INVISIBLE.** The discarded span sits between two fields that both parse correctly, so every field-level check passes and the emitted row is well-formed prose. `unread_field_keys` detects an unrecognised KEY; free prose is not a key, so it fires on nothing here.

**WHY THE HOP's VERIFICATION MISSED IT -- conflab-vc's own certification, in their words, and it is the keeper:** the hop was certified on a census (123/531/133/141, all four matching) plus doctor scanning 1421 files, and **every damaged row is still present.** *A CENSUS ANSWERS WHETHER EVERYTHING IS STILL HERE, NEVER WHETHER ANYTHING IS STILL WHOLE, AND WHEN THE UNIT OF COUNTING IS THE ROW THOSE LOOK IDENTICAL.*

**SCOPE, STATED AS A FLOOR RATHER THAN A COUNT:** "20 rows shortened" is a FLOOR on four threads of one estate. The other 18 shortened rows have not been read -- length is a proxy for loss, not proof of it. **Seventeen estates have been migrated through this parser and none of the others has been checked.**

**THE AUTHORED PROSE IS SAFE where it was preserved:** Conflab's four `acceptance.v2.md` are tracked and committed byte-faithful, sha256-verified against their git blobs. **The risk is that they are never read, because the estate's conventions point at the generated file.** That is not true of every estate: this repository retains no v2 buckets at all, so where the two-homes state was not preserved there is no source to compare against and no route back.
